# ── .env.example ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical reference for all configurable variables in codefreedom.
# This file is tracked in git — update it whenever you add or rename a variable.
#
# ── Layered .env Architecture ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# .env.example       → Template for new setups (tracked in git, NOT used at runtime)
# .env               → Your active config: database, model aliases (git-ignored)
# .env.secrets       → Your API keys, tokens, passwords (NEVER committed)
#
# Load order at runtime (later sources override earlier):
#   1. workspace/.env      — defaults: database, URLs, model aliases, proxy settings
#   2. workspace/.env.secrets — secrets: API keys, passwords (skipped if missing)
#   3. System environment  — machine-level overrides (export FOO=bar wins)
#
# This means:
#   - Set defaults in .env, set secrets in .env.secrets
#   - If .env.secrets is missing, provide secrets via system env vars
#   - System env vars always take highest priority
#
# Quickstart:
#   cp .env.example .env                 # edit with your settings
#   cp .env.secrets.example .env.secrets # edit with your real secrets
#   pip install -e .                     # install codefreedom CLI
#   docker compose up -d                 # start LiteLLM proxy
#   codefreedom claude                   # launch Claude Code
#
# Sections:
#   1. Database
#   2. LiteLLM Proxy
#   3. Model Aliases
#   4. Cloud Provider Base URLs
#   5. OpenAI-Compatible Endpoint
#   6. Anthropic-Compatible Endpoint
#   7. Local Backends
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 1. Database
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── No Database (default) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The proxy runs stateless — no persistence, no Prisma, no Admin UI.
# Model routing and master-key auth work. Leave DATABASE_URL unset.
#
# ── PostgreSQL (opt-in) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# To enable spend tracking, key management, and the Admin UI, uncomment BOTH:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://litellm_interface:${LITELLM_DB_PASSWORD}@postgres:5432/litellm_interface
# Also update litellm/config/config.yaml:
#   - Uncomment: database_url: os.environ/DATABASE_URL
#   - Change: store_model_in_db: false → true
#   - Change: store_prompts_in_spend_logs: false → true


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 2. LiteLLM Proxy — core proxy settings
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Container ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker image to pull (default: docker.litellm.ai/berriai/litellm:latest)
# LITELLM_IMAGE=docker.litellm.ai/berriai/litellm:latest
# LITELLM_CONTAINER_NAME=litellm-codefreedom
# LITELLM_DATA_VOLUME=codefreedom-litellm-data

# ── Networking ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LITELLM_PORT=4000
# Bind address: 127.0.0.1 = local-only, 0.0.0.0 = expose on network
# LITELLM_BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0

# ── Observability ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Log level: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR
# LITELLM_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Disable built-in Swagger/ReDoc UI (recommended for production)
# LITELLM_NO_DOCS="True"
# LITELLM_NO_REDOC="True"
# Log in JSON format (easier to parse with log aggregators)
# LITELLM_JSON_LOGS=true
# Require auth for the /metrics endpoint
# LITELLM_REQUIRE_AUTH_METRICS=false

# ── Privacy / Logging ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Strip unsupported params before forwarding to providers
# LITELLM_DROP_PARAMS=true
# Redact API key info from logs
# LITELLM_REDACT_USER_API_KEY=true
# Disable message content logging (WARNING: enable only for RLHF datasets;
# full conversations may contain sensitive data)
# LITELLM_TURN_OFF_MSG_LOGGING=false
# Log stream usage (tokens consumed per chunk) to the database
# LITELLM_STREAM_USAGE=true

# ── Retry / Resilience ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LITELLM_NUM_RETRIES=5                # Retries for transient failures
# LITELLM_RETRY_AFTER=0                # Cooldown (seconds) before retrying
# LITELLM_TIMEOUT_ERROR_RETRIES=5      # Retries for timeout errors
# LITELLM_RATE_LIMIT_ERROR_RETRIES=5   # Retries for rate-limit (429)
# LITELLM_INTERNAL_ERROR_RETRIES=5     # Retries for internal server errors (5xx)


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 3. Model Aliases
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Model aliases map short CodeFreedom/ names to specific provider models.
# Claude Code discovers these aliases and presents them as available models.
#
# Each alias must match a model_name from your provider YAML files
# (in litellm/config/providers/).
#
# Default: all point to DeepSeek cloud models.
# To use local:   set to "DGX/Qwen3.6-27B" or your local model name.
# To use OpenAI-compatible: set to "OpenAI-Compatible/Default".

# Ultra  — best reasoning, architecture, planning
# LITELLM_MODEL_ALIAS_ULTRA="DeepSeek/DeepSeek-V4-Pro"

# Pro    — implementation, coding work
# LITELLM_MODEL_ALIAS_PRO="DeepSeek/DeepSeek-V4-Flash"

# Flash  — fast, cheap tasks
# LITELLM_MODEL_ALIAS_FLASH="DeepSeek/DeepSeek-V4-Flash"

# Air    — lightweight scanning, mechanical tasks (optional)
# LITELLM_MODEL_ALIAS_AIR="DeepSeek/DeepSeek-V4-Flash"


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 4. Cloud Provider — Base URLs
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Set the matching API key in .env.secrets to enable a provider.
# Leave the key empty to disable. Leave these URLs at their defaults.
#
# To fully disable a cloud provider:
#   1. Leave its API key empty in .env.secrets
#   2. (Optional) Comment out its include line in litellm/config/config.yaml

# DeepSeek — V4 Pro (reasoning) + V4 Flash (fast)
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com

# Microsoft Foundry (Azure AI) — Kimi K2.6, DeepSeek V4 Flash
# MICROSOFT_FOUNDRY_API_BASE=https://<space>.services.ai.azure.com/openai/v1

# NVIDIA AI Endpoints — DeepSeek V4 Flash, MiniMax M2.7, Kimi K2.6
# NVIDIA_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1

# OpenCode Zen — MIMO V2.5, NEMOTRON-3 Super (free tier available)
# OPENCODE_ZEN_BASE_URL=https://opencode.ai/zen/v1


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 5. OpenAI-Compatible Endpoint (bring your own model)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Use this for ANY backend that speaks the OpenAI /v1/chat/completions protocol:
#   - Self-hosted inference servers (Ollama, vLLM, etc.)
#   - Third-party proxies or API gateways
#
# To enable:
#   1. Uncomment the variables below
#   2. Uncomment "providers/openai-compatible.yaml" in litellm/config/config.yaml
#   3. Uncomment the OPENAI_COMPAT_* block in litellm/docker-compose.litellm.yml
#   4. Set OPENAI_COMPAT_API_KEY in .env.secrets
#   5. Restart: docker compose down && docker compose up -d
#
# See docs/configuration.md for full step-by-step.

# OPENAI_COMPAT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
# OPENAI_COMPAT_MODEL=openai/your-model-name


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 6. Anthropic-Compatible Endpoint (bring your own model)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Use this for ANY backend that speaks the Anthropic /v1/messages protocol:
#   - Self-hosted servers with Anthropic API compatibility
#   - Third-party proxies that speak the Anthropic protocol
#
# To enable:
#   1. Uncomment the variables below
#   2. Uncomment "providers/anthropic-compatible.yaml" in litellm/config/config.yaml
#   3. Uncomment the ANTHROPIC_COMPAT_* block in litellm/docker-compose.litellm.yml
#   4. Set ANTHROPIC_COMPAT_API_KEY in .env.secrets
#   5. Restart: docker compose down && docker compose up -d
#
# See docs/configuration.md for full step-by-step.

# ANTHROPIC_COMPAT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
# ANTHROPIC_COMPAT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 7. Local Backends (pre-configured, two ports)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Two pre-configured backends for self-hosted OpenAI-compatible inference.
# Uses providers/local.yaml. Enable by setting API keys in .env.secrets.
#
# If you only have one backend, leave the other API key empty in .env.secrets.
# Cloud-only users: leave both API keys empty and comment out providers/local.yaml
# in litellm/config/config.yaml.

# Backend M (port 8000) — typically a larger model for Pro-tier tasks
# LOCAL_M_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8000/v1
# LOCAL_M_MODEL=openai/qwen3.6_27b

# Backend S (port 8001) — typically a faster model for Flash-tier tasks
# LOCAL_S_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8001/v1
# LOCAL_S_MODEL=openai/qwen3.6_35b_a3b
